**Given:**

Selling Price (SP) = ₹247.50

Gain Percentage = 12.5%

**Formula used:**

Cost Price (CP) = dfrac{SP}{1 + (Gain \%)/(100)}

**Calculation:**

CP = dfrac{247.50}{1 + (12.5)/(100)}

⇒ CP = dfrac{247.50}{1 + 0.125}

⇒ CP = dfrac{247.50}{1.125}

⇒ CP = ₹220

**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**
